            0.244,
            0.092,
            0.386,
            0.115
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Snapshots"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.129,
            0.652,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pressure is defined as force per unit area."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.148,
            0.863,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The SI unit of pressure is newton/metre2 (N/m2) and is also called pascal denoted by Pa."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.185,
            0.819,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Liquids and gases exert pressure on the walls of a container."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.204,
            0.864,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The pressure exerted by the air around us is known as atmospheric pressure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.249,
            0.241,
            0.709,
            0.259
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Differences in air pressure cause winds to blow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.249,
            0.26,
            0.863,
            0.295
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Warm air rises, creating a low-pressure area. Cooler air from surrounding higher-pressure regions moves in to take its place."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.249,
            0.297,
            0.863,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Important requirements for the formation of thunderstorms are moisture and strong winds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.249,
            0.333,
            0.864,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Strong winds moving upwards and downwards facilitate rubbing of ice particles with water droplets, causing electric charges to develop in clouds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.249,
            0.385,
            0.864,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Collision of electric charges within a clouds, or between clouds, or between a cloud and the ground causes lightning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.422,
            0.811,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Lightning strikes can cause destruction to life and property."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.441,
            0.865,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Lightning conductors protect buildings from the effects of lightning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.477,
            0.864,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The India Meteorological Department (IMD) constantly monitors cyclones and thunderstorms in India."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.289,
            0.558,
            0.604,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Keep the curiosity alive"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.594,
            0.587,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": [
